{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-122608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & =-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j"] ["math" "x{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2y{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122608" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122607" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2y+1}}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+1}}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122607" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y) \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122600" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122600" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122600" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(z+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+(x+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k"] ["math" "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k"] ["math" "z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k"] ["math" "z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122600" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{z-2y} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i-\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122404" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,k"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,k"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{2y-z}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122404" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122596" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+2y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+2z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2xz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k"] ["math" "yz\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+xz\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+xy\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122596" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2y-x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-x) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-x) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,2),$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =-i+2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/0f45b194df67a060c195d4368050cdad9b8bfefab86b41d5eb63723631543d7b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/6c76d43daa86b2c8034e3f12592ee6c18bc533034cb255934ff7eb08b2d53623.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/7618ae208ba53f12fb31988a3e0d0cb40f78ddc4348c5049bb09127039c4d965.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/df6472974d246217341c69163c2336190980b5aacaa5b1a5c11cbb7126ddde86.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i+2y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(3,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-4,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,-1) & =i+2\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/0d5f1fb1b13459937f7bd3ff0ed8b6da641fcd346dc961d7ec5b98be29e45b1d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/8a35641fa57b01a95a0c1d5b3dba8a0072b291a6822ac7b2f5e0473b9037796b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/acb2066428e0660e7d4e106acd5faf60600d6f93de0b6cf4c43ee2b5864e6e51.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/cdebaf3d8c07fe6cb26c4fb2c5b72d2bd60dc968b3345fc1c4a5737d8c6c2b53.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122619" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),$ $(0,-2),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,1) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,j=i-j \\\\ ∇f(0,-2) & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-2)}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,j=-4\\,i \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,j=4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122713" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1e9b6c550e79abfd03d4ab0c0c7942b5185d24fd2e72203d1cb87c0895e3a6f4.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/5e19f0874cbbfcf99c45951c98b19d941c39451c33887fbdcacdb75faeffdc57.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/8270942dbaed9f5177e179104bb479802a39c48afa2a528b138b458c042a1556.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/abdb12ae2b6a67283ae65485e124b2a5264ab63a401e8993829f8b56704af479.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122713" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,-3),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-2)^{2}\\,i-2\\,j=3\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-3) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\,i-(-3)\\,j=3\\,i+3\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\,i-\\,j=3\\,i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/4be9586aaa886ccfe092f93c106a5f7233509c798c9a90ecfda0363173dc7afb.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/6cf967e8a5d3bc7b2ac021414875f5221ef52790dfbdd6e214cccc7f0e8be2d2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/9593ba00b964194c1d91549fe38a1334a478ffd6b724534c4512a11d19d683aa.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/f814f8c7e6d879cbe25e5108704e29464d0c39859371ee4fac3bfb3e72f90696.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122789" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2(y-2x) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =y-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-2(y-2x)\\,i+(y-2x)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,1),$ $(1,3),$ and $(-2,-3).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,1) & =-2\\cdot (1-2\\cdot 1)\\,i+(1-2\\cdot 1)\\,j=2\\,i-j \\\\ ∇f(1,3) & =-2\\cdot (3-2\\cdot 1)\\,i+(3-2\\cdot 1)\\,j=-2\\,i+j \\\\ ∇f(-2,-3) & =-2\\cdot (-3-2\\cdot (-2))\\,i+(-3-2\\cdot (-2))\\,j=-2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "291ee631bf62fbaa8e8842bd258b564692b21cc9a695ab81dd4f261b64e27ac2"} {"question" "q-122738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a225ec7db72d7066c66de8a1367f4d7f6b8d1bec970713249a932014c85b"} {"question" "q-122738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/135122e85da455699e45c1e276152b20fee0ac9d18441eb5620b1aa43654c81b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/3bf6311586ae40bb490414108bbf232f40e1e727da45bbdbe3123e60c17f6268.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/716f99a985d8b4909e76f922fc3bf5b3350f9cb7496ae0a0a429421016a19267.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/assets/e4f9011d4497ac01495c1dcde81d9ba19e9b48f9d78c36ca6259d3a2465983b7.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044724/state.json" "file_sha256" "9616a2